    "body": "## Security repair\n\n- Task ID: `user-authorized-security-ui-dm-game-state-repair-20260801-01`\n- Baseline commit: `db54b15ea65226d7513fa38e0fc788452bd3bff6`\n- Head commit: `4e4081169eab2f023ad328f48344f10ae7d7adb0`\n\n### Scope\n\nExactly these five paths changed:\n\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/index.html`\n- `docs/index.html`\n- `tools/test_step9_security_audit_self_trigger.py`\n\nThe repair replaces protected `Game.State` identity reads with `Game.__S.me.id` in the DM respect hooks. The visibility predicate remains pure, and the click hook retains `Game.StateAPI.giveRespect(meId, targetId, timestamp)` as its mutation boundary.\n\nFocused regression coverage asserts the exact actor-ID read in both mirrors, rejects protected `Game.State` access and `Game.__S` mutation patterns, requires the click mutation boundary, and prohibits that mutation call in the pure visibility predicate.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- Independent read-only review: `NO_REVIEW_FINDINGS`; `INDEPENDENT_SECURITY_REVIEW_PASS`.\n- User-owned Safari security regression passed against `4e4081169eab2f023ad328f48344f10ae7d7adb0`.\n- `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest tools.test_step9_security_audit_self_trigger tools.test_step9_ui_boot_forbidden_state_access` — 8 passed, 1 skipped.\n- `node --check AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-dm.js` and `node --check docs/ui/ui-dm.js` passed.\n- Mirror parity and `git diff --check` passed.\n\nNo unrelated implementation change occurred.\n\n### Nonblocking UX observations — out of scope\n\n- The Gen Z respect label remains `Уважение`.\n- Respect-button typography differs from neighboring controls.\n- The points toast appears before the displayed balance value updates.",
